PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L03U1.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":3,"cefr":"A2a","unit":1,"theme":"Then and Now","essential_question":"How has life in our country changed over time?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS1","title":"Grandpa's Old Photos: was and were","objectives":["Students will be able to use was with I/he/she/it and were with you/we/they.","Students will be able to make negatives with wasn't and weren't.","I can say \"The road was dusty\" and \"The houses were small\".","I can say \"It wasn't easy\" and \"They weren't rich\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام was مع I وhe وshe وit وwere مع you وwe وthey.","سيتمكن الطلاب من تكوين النفي باستخدام wasn't وweren't.","أستطيع أن أقول The road was dusty وThe houses were small.","أستطيع أن أقول It wasn't easy وThey weren't rich."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"past","pos":"noun","ipa":"/pæst/","definition":"the time before now","arabic":"الماضي","example":"In the past, people traveled by camel.","image_id":"GV-L03-U1-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS1-W01"},{"word":"present","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈprɛzənt/","definition":"the time now","arabic":"الحاضر","example":"In the present, we travel by car and plane.","image_id":"GV-L03-U1-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS1-W02"},{"word":"ago","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/əˈɡoʊ/","definition":"before now (ten years ago = ten years before today)","arabic":"منذ / قبل","example":"My family moved here five years ago.","image_id":"GV-L03-U1-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS1-W03"},{"word":"modern","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈmɑdɚn/","definition":"new and using the latest ideas","arabic":"حديث / عصري","example":"Riyadh has many modern towers.","image_id":"GV-L03-U1-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"was and were are the past forms of am/is/are. We use them to describe people, places and things in the past: The road was dusty. The houses were small.\nUse was with I, he, she, it and one person or thing. Use were with you, we, they and plural nouns.\nNegative: wasn't (was not) and weren't (were not). Time words like yesterday, last year, in 1965 and ten years ago tell us it is the past.\nI / he / she / it / one thing → was: It was hot.\nyou / we / they / plural → were: They were friends.\nNegative: wasn't / weren't: The road wasn't wide.\nam/is → was; are → were","examples":["My grandpa was a farmer.","The old market was very busy.","We were at the museum yesterday.","The houses were close together.","It wasn't cold last night.","My parents were students in Jeddah in 2005.","The lanes in the village weren't wide.","I was seven years old five years ago."],"common_errors":["✗ Yesterday I am at the park. → ✓ Yesterday I was at the park. (yesterday → past → was.)","✗ They was happy. → ✓ They were happy. (they → were.)","✗ The road not was wide. → ✓ The road wasn't wide. (Negative: was + not (wasn't).)","✗ Grandpa farmer in the past. → ✓ Grandpa was a farmer in the past. (English needs a verb: was.)"],"arabic":"was وwere هما الماضي من am/is/are، ونستخدمهما لوصف الأشياء في الماضي.\nwas مع I وhe وshe وit والمفرد، وwere مع you وwe وthey والجمع.\nالنفي: wasn't وweren't.\nكلمات مثل yesterday وlast year وago تدل على الماضي."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Grandpa's Old Photos: was and were”. Let’s learn past simple of be: was / were / wasn't / weren't together.","on_screen":"GV-L03-U1-LS1 | Grandpa's Old Photos: was and were","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Grandpa's Old Photos”: Last night, Grandpa Saleh showed me some old photos. \"This was my school in 1965,\" he said. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Last night, Grandpa Saleh showed me some old photos. \"This was my school in 1965,\" he said.","visual":"Image GV-L03-U1-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"was and were are the past forms of am/is/are. We use them to describe people, places and things in the past: The road was dusty. The houses were small. Use was with I, he, she, it and one person or thing. Use were with you, we, they and plural nouns.","on_screen":"I / he / she / it / one thing → was: It was hot. • you / we / they / plural → were: They were friends. • Negative: wasn't / weren't: The road wasn't wide.","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. My grandpa was a farmer. The old market was very busy. We were at the museum yesterday.","on_screen":"My grandpa was a farmer. / The old market was very busy. / We were at the museum yesterday.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Yesterday I am at the park.” That’s not right. We say: “Yesterday I was at the park.” yesterday → past → was.","on_screen":"✗ Yesterday I am at the park.   ✓ Yesterday I was at the park.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"The houses were small.\" Is this about now or the past? … Think! … The past. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"The road was dusty\" and \"The houses were small\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"The road was dusty\" and \"The houses were small\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: past simple of be: was / were / wasn't / weren't.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","was وwere هما الماضي من am/is/are، ونستخدمهما لوصف الأشياء في الماضي.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Yesterday I am at the park. — الصحيح: Yesterday I was at the park.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول The road was dusty وThe houses were small."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Grandpa's Old Photos","body":"Last night, Grandpa Saleh showed me some old photos. \"This was my school in 1965,\" he said.\nIt was a small stone building with only two classrooms. The teachers were strict, but they were kind too.\nGrandpa's best friend was a boy called Hamdan. They were always together.\n\"Was life difficult?\" I asked.\n\"Sometimes it was hard,\" Grandpa said. \"There wasn't any electricity in our village, and the roads weren't wide. But we were happy.\"\nToday, Taif is a big, modern city, but I love Grandpa's memories of the past.","word_count":90,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"My grandpa ___ a teacher in the past.","options":["was","is","are","were"],"answer":"was","explanation":"I / he / she / it / one thing → was.","explanation_ar":"was مع المفرد."},{"q":"The streets ___ quiet in 1970.","options":["are","is","was","were"],"answer":"were","explanation":"you / we / they / plural → were.","explanation_ar":"were مع الجمع وyou."},{"q":"Yesterday it ___ very windy.","options":["were","is","was","be"],"answer":"was","explanation":"Past time words (yesterday, last…, ago) → was/were.","explanation_ar":"كلمات الماضي ← was/were."},{"q":"We ___ at the mosque at six.","options":["are","was","is","were"],"answer":"were","explanation":"you / we / they / plural → were.","explanation_ar":"were مع الجمع وyou."},{"q":"The village ___ big. It was small.","options":["not","wasn't","weren't","isn't"],"answer":"wasn't","explanation":"Negative: wasn't / weren't.","explanation_ar":"النفي: wasn't وweren't."},{"q":"My cousins ___ at school yesterday. They were sick.","options":["aren't","wasn't","weren't","not"],"answer":"weren't","explanation":"Negative: wasn't / weren't.","explanation_ar":"النفي: wasn't وweren't."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS1-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Change the sentences to the past.","items":[{"q":"The market is busy.  (past (yesterday))","options":[],"answer":"The market was busy.","explanation":"I / he / she / it / one thing → was.","explanation_ar":"was مع المفرد."},{"q":"The roads are dusty.  (past (in the past))","options":[],"answer":"The roads were dusty.","explanation":"you / we / they / plural → were.","explanation_ar":"were مع الجمع وyou."},{"q":"I am not tired.  (past (last night))","options":[],"answer":"I wasn't tired.","explanation":"Negative: wasn't / weren't.","explanation_ar":"النفي: wasn't وweren't."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS1-B2","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write was, were, wasn't or weren't. Word bank: wasn't, were, was","items":[{"q":"Ten years ago, there ______ a small shop here.","options":[],"answer":"was","explanation":"I / he / she / it / one thing → was.","explanation_ar":"was مع المفرد."},{"q":"My parents ______ in Riyadh last week.","options":[],"answer":"were","explanation":"you / we / they / plural → were.","explanation_ar":"were مع الجمع وyou."},{"q":"The test ______ difficult. It was easy!","options":[],"answer":"wasn't","explanation":"Negative: wasn't / weren't.","explanation_ar":"النفي: wasn't وweren't."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about the past.","items":[{"q":"When I was five, I was ___.","options":[],"answer":"When I was five, I was very shy.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past simple of be: was / were / wasn't / weren't correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Yesterday, the weather was ___.","options":[],"answer":"Yesterday, the weather was sunny.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past simple of be: was / were / wasn't / weren't correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My first teacher was ___.","options":[],"answer":"My first teacher was Mr. Saad.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past simple of be: was / were / wasn't / weren't correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Last Friday, my family and I were ___.","options":[],"answer":"Last Friday, my family and I were at the farm.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past simple of be: was / were / wasn't / weren't correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My favorite toy was ___.","options":[],"answer":"My favorite toy was a red car.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past simple of be: was / were / wasn't / weren't correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Then and now.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 sentences about you when you were small and 1 about you now.","options":[],"answer":"When I was small, I was afraid of the dark. My hair was long. My best friend was Rakan. Now I am brave!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past simple of be: was / were / wasn't / weren't correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about your town in the past. Use wasn't or weren't.","options":[],"answer":"There wasn't a big mall. The roads weren't wide.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past simple of be: was / were / wasn't / weren't correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask a family member about his childhood. Write 2 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"My dad was a good footballer. His school was near the sea.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past simple of be: was / were / wasn't / weren't correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spin & Speak","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Work in teams of four. Player 1 spins the wheel.","Make a correct sentence about the unit theme using the cue word and past simple of be: was / were / wasn't / weren't.","The team checks the sentence with the grammar box. Correct = 1 point; an extra detail = 1 bonus point.","Pass the spinner clockwise. Play for 6 minutes; the team with most points wins."],"data":[{"label":"I"},{"label":"my grandpa"},{"label":"the houses"},{"label":"Taif"},{"label":"we"},{"label":"the road"},{"label":"my parents"},{"label":"the school"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The old house ___ made of mud.","options":["were","be","was","is"],"answer":"was","explanation":"I / he / she / it / one thing → was.","explanation_ar":"was مع المفرد."},{"q":"My grandparents ___ very kind neighbors.","options":["be","were","was","is"],"answer":"were","explanation":"you / we / they / plural → were.","explanation_ar":"were مع الجمع وyou."},{"q":"Last night, I ___ very tired.","options":["am","is","were","was"],"answer":"was","explanation":"Past time words (yesterday, last…, ago) → was/were.","explanation_ar":"كلمات الماضي ← was/were."},{"q":"","options":["The lanes weren't not wide.","The lanes wasn't wide.","The lanes not were wide.","The lanes weren't wide."],"answer":"The lanes weren't wide.","explanation":"Negative: wasn't / weren't.","explanation_ar":"النفي: wasn't وweren't."},{"q":"","options":["We were at the beach two days ago.","We was at the beach two days ago.","We are at the beach two days ago.","We were at the beach two days before ago."],"answer":"We were at the beach two days ago.","explanation":"you / we / they / plural → were.","explanation_ar":"were مع الجمع وyou."},{"q":"In 1990, my mother ___ a student.","options":["was","were","are","is"],"answer":"was","explanation":"I / he / she / it / one thing → was.","explanation_ar":"was مع المفرد."},{"q":"The shop ___ open yesterday. It was closed.","options":["not","isn't","weren't","wasn't"],"answer":"wasn't","explanation":"Negative: wasn't / weren't.","explanation_ar":"النفي: wasn't وweren't."},{"q":"","options":["You were the best player in the match!","You was the best player in the match!","You is the best player in the match!","You were best player the in match!"],"answer":"You were the best player in the match!","explanation":"you / we / they / plural → were.","explanation_ar":"were مع الجمع وyou."},{"q":"","options":["My first phone is old-fashioned last year.","My first phone were old-fashioned.","My first phone was old-fashioned.","My first phone old-fashioned was."],"answer":"My first phone was old-fashioned.","explanation":"I / he / she / it / one thing → was.","explanation_ar":"was مع المفرد."},{"q":"The children ___ in the garden at four.","options":["was","were","is","be"],"answer":"were","explanation":"you / we / they / plural → were.","explanation_ar":"were مع الجمع وyou."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Noura sitting beside Grandpa Saleh on a majlis cushion, looking at black-and-white photos of a small stone school, dusty roads and two boys laughing. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Noura sitting beside Grandpa Saleh on a majlis cushion, looking at black-and-white photos of a small stone school, dusty roads and two boys laughing"},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about past simple of be: was / were / wasn't / weren't, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about past simple of be: was / were / wasn't / weren't, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right"},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows past (the time before now); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing past: the time before now"},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows present (the time now); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing present: the time now"},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows ago (before now (ten years ago = ten years before today)); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing ago: before now (ten years ago = ten years before today)"},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows modern (new and using the latest ideas); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing modern: new and using the latest ideas"},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spin & Speak”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spin & Speak"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS1-W01","script":"past. past. In the past, people traveled by camel.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS1-W02","script":"present. present. In the present, we travel by car and plane.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS1-W03","script":"ago. ago. My family moved here five years ago.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS1-W04","script":"modern. modern. Riyadh has many modern towers.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS1-T1","script":"Last night, Grandpa Saleh showed me some old photos. \"This was my school in 1965,\" he said. It was a small stone building with only two classrooms. The teachers were strict, but they were kind too. Grandpa's best friend was a boy called Hamdan. They were always together. \"Was life difficult?\" I asked. \"Sometimes it was hard,\" Grandpa said. \"There wasn't any electricity in our village, and the roads weren't wide. But we were happy.\" Today, Taif is a big, modern city, but I love Grandpa's memories of the past.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Grandpa's Old Photos: was and were”. Let’s learn past simple of be: was / were / wasn't / weren't together. Listen to the start of “Grandpa's Old Photos”: Last night, Grandpa Saleh showed me some old photos. \"This was my school in 1965,\" he said. Look at the green words. was and were are the past forms of am/is/are. We use them to describe people, places and things in the past: The road was dusty. The houses were small. Use was with I, he, she, it and one person or thing. Use were with you, we, they and plural nouns. Here are some examples. My grandpa was a farmer. The old market was very busy. We were at the museum yesterday. Be careful! Some learners say: “Yesterday I am at the park.” That’s not right. We say: “Yesterday I was at the park.” yesterday → past → was. Quick check: \"The houses were small.\" Is this about now or the past? … Think! … The past. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"The road was dusty\" and \"The houses were small\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS2","title":"There Was a Market Here: there was / there were and Questions","objectives":["Students will be able to use there was and there were to describe places in the past.","Students will be able to ask and answer questions with was and were.","I can say \"There was a market here\" and \"There weren't any cars\".","I can ask \"Where were you?\" and \"Was it fun?\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام there was وthere were لوصف الأماكن في الماضي.","سيتمكن الطلاب من طرح أسئلة بـ was وwere والإجابة عنها.","أستطيع أن أقول There was a market here وThere weren't any cars.","أستطيع أن أسأل Where were you? وWas it fun?"],"vocabulary":[{"word":"old-fashioned","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/oʊldˈfæʃənd/","definition":"not modern; from the past","arabic":"قديم الطراز","example":"My grandma has an old-fashioned radio.","image_id":"GV-L03-U1-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS2-W01"},{"word":"village","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈvɪlədʒ/","definition":"a very small town in the countryside","arabic":"قرية","example":"My grandfather grew up in a mountain village.","image_id":"GV-L03-U1-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS2-W02"},{"word":"building","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbɪldɪŋ/","definition":"a structure with walls and a roof, like a house or a school","arabic":"مبنى","example":"The new hospital is a tall building.","image_id":"GV-L03-U1-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS2-W03"},{"word":"stone","pos":"noun","ipa":"/stoʊn/","definition":"a hard material from rocks","arabic":"حجر","example":"The old fort is made of stone.","image_id":"GV-L03-U1-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"there was (one thing) and there were (many things) are the past of there is and there are: There was a well in the village. There were many palm trees.\nNegative: There wasn't a hospital. There weren't any cars.\nQuestions: put was/were first: Was it fun? – Yes, it was. Were they at home? – No, they weren't. With question words: Where were you yesterday? Why was he late?","examples":["There was a big well in the middle of the village.","There were no paved roads.","There wasn't a supermarket near Grandpa's house.","Were there any schools for girls? – Yes, there were.","Was the trip long? – Yes, it was.","Where were you at five o'clock? – I was at the library.","Was your grandmother a teacher? – No, she wasn't.","Why were the shops closed? – Because it was Friday."],"common_errors":["✗ There was many people. → ✓ There were many people. (Plural → there were.)","✗ In my village had a well. → ✓ There was a well in my village. (Use there was, not had.)","✗ Where you were yesterday? → ✓ Where were you yesterday? (Question: were before you.)","✗ Was they at school? → ✓ Were they at school? (they → were.)"],"arabic":"there was للمفرد وthere were للجمع، وهما الماضي من there is وthere are.\nالنفي: there wasn't وthere weren't any.\nالسؤال: نقدّم was أو were: Was it fun? / Where were you?\nلا نقول In my village had a well، بل There was a well in my village."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “There Was a Market Here: there was / there were and Questions”. Let’s learn there was / there were; questions with was/were (Was it…? Were they…? Where were you?) together.","on_screen":"GV-L03-U1-LS2 | There Was a Market Here: there was / there were and Questions","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: There was a well. • There were camels in the market. There wasn't a mall. • There weren't any traffic lights. Was there a school? – Yes, there was. • Were there any cars? – No, there weren't. • Where were you? – I was at Grandpa's.","on_screen":"There was a well. • There were camels in the market. | There wasn't a mall. • There weren't any traffic lights. | Was there a school? – Yes, there was. • Were there any cars? – No, there weren't. • Where were you? – I was at Grandpa's.","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"there was (one thing) and there were (many things) are the past of there is and there are: There was a well in the village. There were many palm trees. Negative: There wasn't a hospital. There weren't any cars.","on_screen":"there was / there were; questions with was/were (Was it…? Were they…? Where were you?)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. There was a big well in the middle of the village. There were no paved roads. There wasn't a supermarket near Grandpa's house.","on_screen":"There was a big well in the middle of the village. / There were no paved roads. / There wasn't a supermarket near Grandpa's house.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “There was many people.” That’s not right. We say: “There were many people.” Plural → there were.","on_screen":"✗ There was many people.   ✓ There were many people.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"There were many palm trees.\" One tree or many? … Think! … Many. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"There was a market here\" and \"There weren't any cars\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"There was a market here\" and \"There weren't any cars\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: there was / there were; questions with was/were (Was it…? Were they…? Where were you?).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","there was للمفرد وthere were للجمع، وهما الماضي من there is وthere are.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: There was many people. — الصحيح: There were many people.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول There was a market here وThere weren't any cars."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"___ a small shop on the corner.","options":["There were","It was","Was there","There was"],"answer":"There was","explanation":"One thing → there was.","explanation_ar":"للمفرد: there was."},{"q":"___ many camels in the old market.","options":["Were there","There were","There was","It were"],"answer":"There were","explanation":"Many things → there were.","explanation_ar":"للجمع: there were."},{"q":"___ the museum interesting? – Yes, it was.","options":["Was","Were","Is","Did"],"answer":"Was","explanation":"Questions: Was/Were + subject…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال يبدأ بـ was أو were."},{"q":"Where ___ you last night?","options":["did","are","were","was"],"answer":"were","explanation":"Where/Why/When + was/were + subject?","explanation_ar":"أداة الاستفهام ثم was/were ثم الفاعل."},{"q":"Were your cousins at the wedding? – Yes, they ___.","options":["did","were","was","are"],"answer":"were","explanation":"Short answers: Yes, it was. / No, they weren't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة."},{"q":"There ___ any traffic lights in the village.","options":["weren't","didn't","aren't","wasn't"],"answer":"weren't","explanation":"Many things → there were.","explanation_ar":"للجمع: there were."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS2-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Make questions.","items":[{"q":"The film was long.  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Was the film long?","explanation":"Questions: Was/Were + subject…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال يبدأ بـ was أو were."},{"q":"There were trees in the old street.  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Were there trees in the old street?","explanation":"Questions: Was/Were + subject…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال يبدأ بـ was أو were."},{"q":"You were at the park. (Where)","options":[],"answer":"Where were you?","explanation":"Where/Why/When + was/were + subject?","explanation_ar":"أداة الاستفهام ثم was/were ثم الفاعل."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS2-B2","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write there was or there were. Word bank: There was, There were, there was","items":[{"q":"In 1960, ______ only one school in our town.","options":[],"answer":"there was","explanation":"One thing → there was.","explanation_ar":"للمفرد: there was."},{"q":"______ no cars in my great-grandfather's village.","options":[],"answer":"There were","explanation":"Many things → there were.","explanation_ar":"للجمع: there were."},{"q":"______ a beautiful fountain in the old square.","options":[],"answer":"There was","explanation":"One thing → there was.","explanation_ar":"للمفرد: there was."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Answer about the past.","items":[{"q":"Where were you last Friday?","options":[],"answer":"I was at my uncle's farm.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses there was / there were; questions with was/were (Was it…? Were they…? Where were you?) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Was your last test easy?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, it was.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses there was / there were; questions with was/were (Was it…? Were they…? Where were you?) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Were your friends at school yesterday?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, they were.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses there was / there were; questions with was/were (Was it…? Were they…? Where were you?) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Was there a park near your first house?","options":[],"answer":"No, there wasn't.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses there was / there were; questions with was/were (Was it…? Were they…? Where were you?) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Who was your first friend?","options":[],"answer":"My first friend was Turki.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses there was / there were; questions with was/were (Was it…? Were they…? Where were you?) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Interview about the past.","items":[{"q":"Write 4 questions to ask an older person about his childhood.","options":[],"answer":"Where were you born? Was there a school in your village? Were there many cars? What was your favorite game?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses there was / there were; questions with was/were (Was it…? Were they…? Where were you?) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences about a place in the past with there was/were.","options":[],"answer":"There was a big well. There were many sheep. There wasn't a hospital.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses there was / there were; questions with was/were (Was it…? Were they…? Where were you?) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Compare a place then and now in 2 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"In the past, there was a small souq here. Now there is a huge mall.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses there was / there were; questions with was/were (Was it…? Were they…? Where were you?) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Tic-Tac-Grammar","mechanic":"tic_tac_toe","rules":["Two teams: X and O. Team X chooses a square.","Using the cue, the team says a correct sentence with there was / there were; questions with was/were (Was it…? Were they…? Where were you?) (the form in brackets: +, – or ?).","If the class and teacher agree it is correct, the team marks the square.","Three squares in a row wins. Play a second round with the grid turned around."],"data":[{"cue":"the streets / narrow / –"},{"cue":"there / a cinema / ?"},{"cue":"my grandparents / at the market / +"},{"cue":"there / many cars / –"},{"cue":"you / at home / yesterday / ?"},{"cue":"the school / small / +"},{"cue":"there / a big mall / –"},{"cue":"your dad / a good student / ?"},{"cue":"the houses / made of stone / +"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"___ a big palm tree in front of our old house.","options":["There was","There were","It was","Was there"],"answer":"There was","explanation":"One thing → there was.","explanation_ar":"للمفرد: there was."},{"q":"___ any cars in the village?","options":["Was there","There was","Were there","There were"],"answer":"Were there","explanation":"Questions: Was/Were + subject…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال يبدأ بـ was أو were."},{"q":"","options":["There were three bakery on this street.","It were three bakeries on this street.","There was three bakeries on this street.","There were three bakeries on this street."],"answer":"There were three bakeries on this street.","explanation":"Many things → there were.","explanation_ar":"للجمع: there were."},{"q":"","options":["Where was your parents in 2010?","Where your parents were in 2010?","Where were your parents in 2010 was?","Where were your parents in 2010?"],"answer":"Where were your parents in 2010?","explanation":"Where/Why/When + was/were + subject?","explanation_ar":"أداة الاستفهام ثم was/were ثم الفاعل."},{"q":"Was the old school far? – No, it ___.","options":["wasn't","weren't","isn't","didn't"],"answer":"wasn't","explanation":"Short answers: Yes, it was. / No, they weren't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة."},{"q":"","options":["It wasn't a hospital in the town.","There wasn't a hospital in the town.","There not was a hospital in the town.","There weren't a hospital in the town."],"answer":"There wasn't a hospital in the town.","explanation":"One thing → there was.","explanation_ar":"للمفرد: there was."},{"q":"___ the shops open on Friday morning?","options":["Did","Were","Are","Was"],"answer":"Were","explanation":"Questions: Was/Were + subject…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال يبدأ بـ was أو were."},{"q":"","options":["Why were Faisal late yesterday?","Why was late Faisal yesterday?","Why was Faisal late yesterday?","Why Faisal was late yesterday?"],"answer":"Why was Faisal late yesterday?","explanation":"Where/Why/When + was/were + subject?","explanation_ar":"أداة الاستفهام ثم was/were ثم الفاعل."},{"q":"Were there any trains in 1950? – No, there ___.","options":["wasn't","aren't","didn't","weren't"],"answer":"weren't","explanation":"Short answers: Yes, it was. / No, they weren't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة."},{"q":"","options":["In the past, there was a well in every village.","In the past, every village had there a well.","In the past, it was a well in every village.","In the past, there were a well in every village."],"answer":"In the past, there was a well in every village.","explanation":"One thing → there was.","explanation_ar":"للمفرد: there was."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"A split picture of the same street: on the left an old souq with camels and a well in the past, on the right a modern road with cars and a mall today. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A split picture of the same street: on the left an old souq with camels and a well in the past, on the right a modern road with cars and a mall today"},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of there was / there were; questions with was/were (Was it…? Were they…? Where were you?): a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Then and Now”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of there was / there were"},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows old-fashioned (not modern; from the past); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing old-fashioned: not modern; from the past"},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows village (a very small town in the countryside); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing village: a very small town in the countryside"},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows building (a structure with walls and a roof, like a house or a school); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing building: a structure with walls and a roof, like a house or a school"},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows stone (a hard material from rocks); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing stone: a hard material from rocks"},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Tic-Tac-Grammar”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Tic-Tac-Grammar"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS2-W01","script":"old-fashioned. old-fashioned. My grandma has an old-fashioned radio.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS2-W02","script":"village. village. My grandfather grew up in a mountain village.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS2-W03","script":"building. building. The new hospital is a tall building.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS2-W04","script":"stone. stone. The old fort is made of stone.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “There Was a Market Here: there was / there were and Questions”. Let’s learn there was / there were; questions with was/were (Was it…? Were they…? Where were you?) together. Remember these patterns: There was a well. • There were camels in the market. There wasn't a mall. • There weren't any traffic lights. Was there a school? – Yes, there was. • Were there any cars? – No, there weren't. • Where were you? – I was at Grandpa's. there was (one thing) and there were (many things) are the past of there is and there are: There was a well in the village. There were many palm trees. Negative: There wasn't a hospital. There weren't any cars. Here are some examples. There was a big well in the middle of the village. There were no paved roads. There wasn't a supermarket near Grandpa's house. Be careful! Some learners say: “There was many people.” That’s not right. We say: “There were many people.” Plural → there were. Quick check: \"There were many palm trees.\" One tree or many? … Think! … Many. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"There was a market here\" and \"There weren't any cars\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS3","title":"Old and Modern: Describing Then and Now","objectives":["Students will be able to describe places and things with then-and-now adjectives.","Students will be able to use opposites and choose between words with similar meanings (old, old-fashioned, ancient).","I can describe a place in the past and now.","I can choose between old, old-fashioned and ancient."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من وصف الأماكن والأشياء بصفات الماضي والحاضر.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام الأضداد والتمييز بين الكلمات المتقاربة في المعنى.","أستطيع أن أصف مكانًا في الماضي والحاضر.","أستطيع أن أختار بين old وold-fashioned وancient."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"mud","pos":"noun","ipa":"/mʌd/","definition":"wet, soft earth","arabic":"طين","example":"Some old houses in Najd were made of mud.","image_id":"GV-L03-U1-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS3-W01"},{"word":"dusty","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈdʌsti/","definition":"covered with dust; dry and dirty","arabic":"مُغبَرّ","example":"The roads were dusty after the wind.","image_id":"GV-L03-U1-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS3-W02"},{"word":"narrow","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈnɛroʊ/","definition":"not wide; small from side to side","arabic":"ضيق","example":"The old market has narrow lanes.","image_id":"GV-L03-U1-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS3-W03"},{"word":"wide","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/waɪd/","definition":"big from side to side","arabic":"واسع / عريض","example":"King Fahd Road is very wide.","image_id":"GV-L03-U1-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS3-W04"},{"word":"memory","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmɛmɚi/","definition":"something you remember from the past","arabic":"ذكرى","example":"Eid at Grandma's house is my best memory.","image_id":"GV-L03-U1-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS3-W05"}],"explanation":{"text":"To compare then and now, use pairs of opposites: narrow ↔ wide, quiet ↔ busy, modern ↔ old-fashioned, dusty ↔ clean.\nSome words have similar meanings but different strengths. old = not new; old-fashioned = not modern in style; ancient = very, very old (hundreds or thousands of years).\nUse ago after a time: fifty years ago, two days ago. Use in the past and nowadays to compare.\nCollocations/phrases: narrow ↔ wide • quiet ↔ busy/noisy • modern ↔ old-fashioned • dusty ↔ clean • small ↔ huge | old (not new) → old-fashioned (not modern) → ancient (thousands of years old) | in the past • … years ago • long ago • nowadays • today • these days","examples":["The lanes in the old town were narrow.","Nowadays the roads are wide and clean.","Al-Ula has ancient tombs cut in the rocks.","Grandma's kitchen is old-fashioned.","The houses were made of stone and mud.","Long ago, people used camels to travel.","Nowadays, people travel by plane.","Our school has modern computers."],"common_errors":["✗ The ancient phone of my dad. → ✓ My dad's old phone. (ancient is for thousands of years; a phone is just old.)","✗ Before ten years, there was a farm. → ✓ Ten years ago, there was a farm. (Use … ago, not before ….)","✗ The street is very wideness. → ✓ The street is very wide. (Use the adjective wide.)"],"arabic":"لوصف الماضي والحاضر نستخدم الأضداد: narrow (ضيق) ↔ wide (واسع)، modern (حديث) ↔ old-fashioned (قديم الطراز).\nancient تعني «قديم جدًا» (آلاف السنين) مثل آثار العُلا، أما old فتعني «قديم» فقط.\nنقول ten years ago (قبل عشر سنوات) وليس before ten years."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Old and Modern: Describing Then and Now”. Let’s learn adjectives for then and now; opposites; shades of meaning (old → ancient) together.","on_screen":"GV-L03-U1-LS3 | Old and Modern: Describing Then and Now","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. mud: wet, soft earth. dusty: covered with dust; dry and dirty. narrow: not wide; small from side to side.","on_screen":"mud | dusty | narrow","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"To compare then and now, use pairs of opposites: narrow ↔ wide, quiet ↔ busy, modern ↔ old-fashioned, dusty ↔ clean. Some words have similar meanings but different strengths. old = not new; old-fashioned = not modern in style; ancient = very, very old (hundreds or thousands of years).","on_screen":"adjectives for then and now; opposites; shades of meaning (old → ancient)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The lanes in the old town were narrow. Nowadays the roads are wide and clean. Al-Ula has ancient tombs cut in the rocks.","on_screen":"The lanes in the old town were narrow. / Nowadays the roads are wide and clean. / Al-Ula has ancient tombs cut in the rocks.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The ancient phone of my dad.” That’s not right. We say: “My dad's old phone.” ancient is for thousands of years; a phone is just old.","on_screen":"✗ The ancient phone of my dad.   ✓ My dad's old phone.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Is a phone from 2015 \"ancient\"? … Think! … No – it is *old*. Ancient = thousands of years. Great job! Now you can say: I can describe a place in the past and now.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can describe a place in the past and now.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: adjectives for then and now; opposites; shades of meaning (old → ancient).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","لوصف الماضي والحاضر نستخدم الأضداد: narrow (ضيق) ↔ wide (واسع)، modern (حديث) ↔ old-fashioned (قديم الطراز).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The ancient phone of my dad. — الصحيح: My dad's old phone.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أصف مكانًا في الماضي والحاضر."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"narrow ↔ ___","options":["quiet","wide","dusty","ancient"],"answer":"wide","explanation":"Choose the opposite word.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المضادة."},{"q":"modern ↔ ___","options":["wide","clean","old-fashioned","busy"],"answer":"old-fashioned","explanation":"Choose the opposite word.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المضادة."},{"q":"The rock tombs in Al-Ula are 2,000 years old. They are ___.","options":["modern","new","old-fashioned","ancient"],"answer":"ancient","explanation":"old (not new) • old-fashioned (not modern) • ancient (very, very old).","explanation_ar":"درجات المعنى للقِدم."},{"q":"My family moved to Taif three years ___.","options":["before","past","ago","since"],"answer":"ago","explanation":"number + time + ago.","explanation_ar":"العدد ثم الوقت ثم ago."},{"q":"After the sandstorm, the cars were ___.","options":["dusty","ancient","wide","modern"],"answer":"dusty","explanation":"Choose the word that fits the meaning.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة للمعنى."},{"q":"Some old houses in Najd were made of ___.","options":["plastic","paper","glass","mud"],"answer":"mud","explanation":"Choose the word that fits the meaning.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة للمعنى."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the word to the meaning.","items":[{"q":"ancient","options":["thousands of years old","a house, school or tower","something you remember","big from side to side","a very small town","at the present time"],"answer":"thousands of years old","explanation":"ancient → thousands of years old. Choose the opposite word.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المضادة."},{"q":"village","options":["thousands of years old","a house, school or tower","something you remember","big from side to side","a very small town","at the present time"],"answer":"a very small town","explanation":"village → a very small town. Choose the opposite word.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المضادة."},{"q":"memory","options":["thousands of years old","a house, school or tower","something you remember","big from side to side","a very small town","at the present time"],"answer":"something you remember","explanation":"memory → something you remember. Choose the opposite word.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المضادة."},{"q":"nowadays","options":["thousands of years old","a house, school or tower","something you remember","big from side to side","a very small town","at the present time"],"answer":"at the present time","explanation":"nowadays → at the present time. Choose the opposite word.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المضادة."},{"q":"wide","options":["thousands of years old","a house, school or tower","something you remember","big from side to side","a very small town","at the present time"],"answer":"big from side to side","explanation":"wide → big from side to side. Choose the opposite word.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المضادة."},{"q":"building","options":["thousands of years old","a house, school or tower","something you remember","big from side to side","a very small town","at the present time"],"answer":"a house, school or tower","explanation":"building → a house, school or tower. Choose the opposite word.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المضادة."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Describe your town then and now.","items":[{"q":"In the past, my town was ___.","options":[],"answer":"In the past, my town was small and quiet.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adjectives for then and now; opposites; shades of meaning (old → ancient) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Nowadays, my town is ___.","options":[],"answer":"Nowadays, my town is big and busy.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adjectives for then and now; opposites; shades of meaning (old → ancient) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"___ years ago, there was ___.","options":[],"answer":"Ten years ago, there was a small park.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adjectives for then and now; opposites; shades of meaning (old → ancient) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"An ancient place in Saudi Arabia is ___.","options":[],"answer":"An ancient place in Saudi Arabia is Hegra.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adjectives for then and now; opposites; shades of meaning (old → ancient) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"An old-fashioned thing in my house is ___.","options":[],"answer":"An old-fashioned thing in my house is my grandpa's clock.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adjectives for then and now; opposites; shades of meaning (old → ancient) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Make a \"Then and Now\" poster.","items":[{"q":"Draw a place then and now. Label 3 opposites.","options":[],"answer":"narrow road → wide road; mud house → modern house; quiet → busy","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adjectives for then and now; opposites; shades of meaning (old → ancient) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences about your poster.","options":[],"answer":"In the past, the road was narrow. Now it is wide. Long ago, the houses were made of mud.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adjectives for then and now; opposites; shades of meaning (old → ancient) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write about one family memory.","options":[],"answer":"My best memory is camping with my cousins in the desert.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adjectives for then and now; opposites; shades of meaning (old → ancient) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Memory Match","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Place all cards face down in a grid.","Turn over two cards. If the word matches its definition, keep the pair and say a sentence with the word.","If not, turn them back over; the next player plays.","The player with the most pairs wins."],"data":[{"word":"past","match":"the time before now","arabic":"الماضي"},{"word":"present","match":"the time now","arabic":"الحاضر"},{"word":"ago","match":"before now (ten years ago = ten years before today)","arabic":"منذ / قبل"},{"word":"modern","match":"new and using the latest ideas","arabic":"حديث / عصري"},{"word":"old-fashioned","match":"not modern; from the past","arabic":"قديم الطراز"},{"word":"village","match":"a very small town in the countryside","arabic":"قرية"},{"word":"building","match":"a structure with walls and a roof, like a house or a school","arabic":"مبنى"},{"word":"stone","match":"a hard material from rocks","arabic":"حجر"},{"word":"mud","match":"wet, soft earth","arabic":"طين"},{"word":"dusty","match":"covered with dust; dry and dirty","arabic":"مُغبَرّ"},{"word":"narrow","match":"not wide; small from side to side","arabic":"ضيق"},{"word":"wide","match":"big from side to side","arabic":"واسع / عريض"},{"word":"memory","match":"something you remember from the past","arabic":"ذكرى"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"quiet ↔ ___","options":["dusty","busy","ancient","narrow"],"answer":"busy","explanation":"Choose the opposite word.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المضادة."},{"q":"dusty ↔ ___","options":["clean","modern","old","wide"],"answer":"clean","explanation":"Choose the opposite word.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المضادة."},{"q":"A radio from 1980 is ___.","options":["modern","new","old-fashioned","ancient"],"answer":"old-fashioned","explanation":"old (not new) • old-fashioned (not modern) • ancient (very, very old).","explanation_ar":"درجات المعنى للقِدم."},{"q":"","options":["We visited Hegra two months before ago.","We visited Hegra two months ago.","We visited Hegra before two months.","We visited Hegra ago two months."],"answer":"We visited Hegra two months ago.","explanation":"number + time + ago.","explanation_ar":"العدد ثم الوقت ثم ago."},{"q":"Something you remember from the past is a ___.","options":["building","village","memory","stone"],"answer":"memory","explanation":"Choose the word that fits the meaning.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة للمعنى."},{"q":"Which word means \"very, very old\"?","options":["modern","wide","ancient","dusty"],"answer":"ancient","explanation":"old (not new) • old-fashioned (not modern) • ancient (very, very old).","explanation_ar":"درجات المعنى للقِدم."},{"q":"___, people use phones to pay.","options":["Nowadays","Ago","Long ago","In the past"],"answer":"Nowadays","explanation":"Choose the word that fits the meaning.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة للمعنى."},{"q":"The tall glass towers in Riyadh are ___.","options":["ancient","dusty","narrow","modern"],"answer":"modern","explanation":"Choose the opposite word.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المضادة."},{"q":"A very small town in the countryside is a ___.","options":["city","country","building","village"],"answer":"village","explanation":"Choose the word that fits the meaning.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة للمعنى."},{"q":"","options":["The old fort made of stone is.","The old fort is made of stone.","The old fort is made from stones it.","The old fort is made of a stones."],"answer":"The old fort is made of stone.","explanation":"Choose the word that fits the meaning.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة للمعنى."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"Two postcards of the same city: an old one in sepia showing narrow lanes, mud houses and a dusty road, and a new bright one showing wide roads, modern towers and a park. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two postcards of the same city: an old one in sepia showing narrow lanes, mud houses and a dusty road, and a new bright one showing wide roads, modern towers and a park"},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 5 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 5 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows mud (wet, soft earth); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing mud: wet, soft earth"},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows dusty (covered with dust; dry and dirty); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing dusty: covered with dust; dry and dirty"},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows narrow (not wide; small from side to side); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing narrow: not wide; small from side to side"},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows wide (big from side to side); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing wide: big from side to side"},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows memory (something you remember from the past); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing memory: something you remember from the past"},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Memory Match”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Memory Match"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS3-W01","script":"mud. mud. Some old houses in Najd were made of mud.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS3-W02","script":"dusty. dusty. The roads were dusty after the wind.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS3-W03","script":"narrow. narrow. The old market has narrow lanes.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS3-W04","script":"wide. wide. King Fahd Road is very wide.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS3-W05","script":"memory. memory. Eid at Grandma's house is my best memory.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Old and Modern: Describing Then and Now”. Let’s learn adjectives for then and now; opposites; shades of meaning (old → ancient) together. Meet some new words. mud: wet, soft earth. dusty: covered with dust; dry and dirty. narrow: not wide; small from side to side. To compare then and now, use pairs of opposites: narrow ↔ wide, quiet ↔ busy, modern ↔ old-fashioned, dusty ↔ clean. Some words have similar meanings but different strengths. old = not new; old-fashioned = not modern in style; ancient = very, very old (hundreds or thousands of years). Here are some examples. The lanes in the old town were narrow. Nowadays the roads are wide and clean. Al-Ula has ancient tombs cut in the rocks. Be careful! Some learners say: “The ancient phone of my dad.” That’s not right. We say: “My dad's old phone.” ancient is for thousands of years; a phone is just old. Quick check: Is a phone from 2015 \"ancient\"? … Think! … No – it is *old*. Ancient = thousands of years. Great job! Now you can say: I can describe a place in the past and now.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS4","title":"Saudi, Egyptian, Arabic: Capitalizing Proper Nouns","objectives":["Students will be able to capitalize the names of cities, countries, nationalities and languages.","Students will be able to find and correct capitalization mistakes in a paragraph.","I can write \"Saudi\", \"Egyptian\" and \"English\" with capital letters.","I can correct capital-letter mistakes."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة أسماء المدن والدول والجنسيات واللغات بحرف كبير.","سيتمكن الطلاب من تصحيح أخطاء الحروف الكبيرة في فقرة.","أستطيع أن أكتب Saudi وEgyptian وEnglish بحرف كبير.","أستطيع أن أصحح أخطاء الحروف الكبيرة."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"past","pos":"noun","ipa":"/pæst/","definition":"the time before now","arabic":"الماضي","example":"In the past, people traveled by camel.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"present","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈprɛzənt/","definition":"the time now","arabic":"الحاضر","example":"In the present, we travel by car and plane.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"ago","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/əˈɡoʊ/","definition":"before now (ten years ago = ten years before today)","arabic":"منذ / قبل","example":"My family moved here five years ago.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"modern","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈmɑdɚn/","definition":"new and using the latest ideas","arabic":"حديث / عصري","example":"Riyadh has many modern towers.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"old-fashioned","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/oʊldˈfæʃənd/","definition":"not modern; from the past","arabic":"قديم الطراز","example":"My grandma has an old-fashioned radio.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"village","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈvɪlədʒ/","definition":"a very small town in the countryside","arabic":"قرية","example":"My grandfather grew up in a mountain village.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"In English, nationalities and languages always start with a capital letter: Saudi, Egyptian, Jordanian, Malaysian; Arabic, English, French. This is different from Arabic.\nCities and countries also start with a capital letter: Madinah, Saudi Arabia, Egypt, Malaysia.\nThe words city, country, language and nationality are common nouns – they are small letters.\nCountries → Saudi Arabia, Jordan, Malaysia\nCities → Taif, Cairo, Kuala Lumpur\nNationalities → Saudi, Egyptian, Jordanian, Malaysian\nLanguages → Arabic, English, Urdu (and school subjects that are languages)","examples":["Yusuf is Egyptian. He was born in Cairo.","Lina speaks Arabic and English.","Adam is from Kuala Lumpur in Malaysia.","Saudi coffee is famous.","Our English teacher is from Jordan.","My uncle learned French in Paris.","Many Indonesian pilgrims visit Makkah.","The city is beautiful in spring."],"common_errors":["✗ My friend is egyptian. → ✓ My friend is Egyptian. (Nationalities need a capital letter.)","✗ I speak arabic and english. → ✓ I speak Arabic and English. (Languages need capital letters.)","✗ Saudi Arabia is a big Country. → ✓ Saudi Arabia is a big country. (country is a common noun.)","✗ We have english on Monday. → ✓ We have English on Monday. (The language subject needs a capital.)"],"arabic":"في الإنجليزية الجنسيات واللغات تبدأ بحرف كبير: Saudi وArabic وEnglish (بخلاف العربية).\nأسماء المدن والدول بحرف كبير: Cairo وEgypt.\nالكلمات العامة مثل city وcountry تُكتب بحرف صغير."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Saudi, Egyptian, Arabic: Capitalizing Proper Nouns”. Let’s learn capital letters for cities, countries, nationalities and languages together.","on_screen":"GV-L03-U1-LS4 | Saudi, Egyptian, Arabic: Capitalizing Proper Nouns","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"In English, nationalities and languages always start with a capital letter: Saudi, Egyptian, Jordanian, Malaysian; Arabic, English, French. This is different from Arabic.","on_screen":"capital letters for cities, countries, nationalities and languages","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"In English, nationalities and languages always start with a capital letter: Saudi, Egyptian, Jordanian, Malaysian; Arabic, English, French. This is different from Arabic. Cities and countries also start with a capital letter: Madinah, Saudi Arabia, Egypt, Malaysia.","on_screen":"Countries → Saudi Arabia, Jordan, Malaysia • Cities → Taif, Cairo, Kuala Lumpur • Nationalities → Saudi, Egyptian, Jordanian, Malaysian","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Yusuf is Egyptian. He was born in Cairo. Lina speaks Arabic and English. Adam is from Kuala Lumpur in Malaysia.","on_screen":"Yusuf is Egyptian. He was born in Cairo. / Lina speaks Arabic and English. / Adam is from Kuala Lumpur in Malaysia.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “My friend is egyptian.” That’s not right. We say: “My friend is Egyptian.” Nationalities need a capital letter.","on_screen":"✗ My friend is egyptian.   ✓ My friend is Egyptian.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Does \"english\" need a capital letter? … Think! … Yes – *English*. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"Saudi\", \"Egyptian\" and \"English\" with capital letters.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"Saudi\", \"Egyptian\" and \"English\" with capital letters.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: capital letters for cities, countries, nationalities and languages.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","في الإنجليزية الجنسيات واللغات تبدأ بحرف كبير: Saudi وArabic وEnglish (بخلاف العربية).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: My friend is egyptian. — الصحيح: My friend is Egyptian.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب Saudi وEgyptian وEnglish بحرف كبير."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"About Me – Adam (editing passage)","body":"My name is Adam. I am malaysian. I was born in kuala lumpur. Now I live in taif. I speak malay, english and a little Arabic. My best friend is saudi.","word_count":31,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct sentence.","items":[{"q":"","options":["lina is Jordanian.","Lina is jordanian.","Lina is Jordanian.","Lina Is jordanian."],"answer":"Lina is Jordanian.","explanation":"Nationalities start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الجنسيات بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["We learn English and Arabic.","We learn english and arabic.","We learn English and arabic.","We learn english and Arabic."],"answer":"We learn English and Arabic.","explanation":"Languages start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"اللغات بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["Adam lives in malaysia.","adam lives in Malaysia.","Adam Lives in malaysia.","Adam lives in Malaysia."],"answer":"Adam lives in Malaysia.","explanation":"Cities and countries start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"المدن والدول بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["Jeddah is a big City.","jeddah is a big city.","Jeddah Is a big City.","Jeddah is a big city."],"answer":"Jeddah is a big city.","explanation":"city, country, language are common nouns – small letters.","explanation_ar":"الكلمات العامة بحرف صغير."},{"q":"","options":["My neighbor is Indian. He speaks hindi.","My neighbor is indian. He speaks hindi.","My neighbor is Indian. He speaks Hindi.","My neighbor is indian. He speaks Hindi."],"answer":"My neighbor is Indian. He speaks Hindi.","explanation":"Languages start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"اللغات بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["Cairo is the Capital of Egypt.","Cairo is the capital of Egypt.","Cairo is the capital of egypt.","cairo is the capital of egypt."],"answer":"Cairo is the capital of Egypt.","explanation":"Cities and countries start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"المدن والدول بحرف كبير."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the capital letter mistake.","items":[{"q":"My teacher is sudanese.","options":[],"answer":"My teacher is Sudanese.","explanation":"sudanese → Sudanese. Nationalities start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: sudanese → Sudanese. الجنسيات بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Can you speak french?","options":[],"answer":"Can you speak French?","explanation":"french → French. Languages start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: french → French. اللغات بحرف كبير."},{"q":"We flew to jordan last summer.","options":[],"answer":"We flew to Jordan last summer.","explanation":"jordan → Jordan. Cities and countries start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: jordan → Jordan. المدن والدول بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Saudi Arabia is a large Country.","options":[],"answer":"Saudi Arabia is a large country.","explanation":"Country → country. city, country, language are common nouns – small letters.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Country → country. الكلمات العامة بحرف صغير."},{"q":"Our english lesson is at nine.","options":[],"answer":"Our English lesson is at nine.","explanation":"english → English. Languages start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: english → English. اللغات بحرف كبير."},{"q":"My cousin studies in london.","options":[],"answer":"My cousin studies in London.","explanation":"london → London. Cities and countries start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: london → London. المدن والدول بحرف كبير."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit Adam's profile.","items":[{"q":"I am malaysian.","options":[],"answer":"I am Malaysian.","explanation":"malaysian → Malaysian. Nationalities start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: malaysian → Malaysian. الجنسيات بحرف كبير."},{"q":"I was born in kuala lumpur.","options":[],"answer":"I was born in Kuala Lumpur.","explanation":"kuala lumpur → Kuala Lumpur. Nationalities start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: kuala lumpur → Kuala Lumpur. الجنسيات بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Now I live in taif.","options":[],"answer":"Now I live in Taif.","explanation":"taif → Taif. Nationalities start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: taif → Taif. الجنسيات بحرف كبير."},{"q":"I speak malay, English and a little Arabic.","options":[],"answer":"I speak Malay, English and a little Arabic.","explanation":"malay → Malay. Nationalities start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: malay → Malay. الجنسيات بحرف كبير."},{"q":"I speak Malay, english and a little Arabic.","options":[],"answer":"I speak Malay, English and a little Arabic.","explanation":"english → English. Nationalities start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: english → English. الجنسيات بحرف كبير."},{"q":"My best friend is saudi.","options":[],"answer":"My best friend is Saudi.","explanation":"saudi → Saudi. Nationalities start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: saudi → Saudi. الجنسيات بحرف كبير."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write a profile.","items":[{"q":"Write your nationality and the languages you speak.","options":[],"answer":"I am Saudi. I speak Arabic and English.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses capital letters for cities, countries, nationalities and languages correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write about a friend or relative from another country.","options":[],"answer":"My uncle's wife is Moroccan. She speaks Arabic and French.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses capital letters for cities, countries, nationalities and languages correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 countries you want to visit and their languages.","options":[],"answer":"Japan – Japanese; Spain – Spanish; Turkey – Turkish","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses capital letters for cities, countries, nationalities and languages correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Builder","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["The teacher reads a word and a short clue.","Teams build the word with letter tiles in 30 seconds.","The team holds up the word; correct spelling = 1 point, with correct capital letter or punctuation where needed = 1 bonus point.","Continue until all words are used."],"data":[{"word":"Saudi","clue":""},{"word":"Egyptian","clue":""},{"word":"Jordanian","clue":""},{"word":"Malaysian","clue":""},{"word":"Arabic","clue":""},{"word":"English","clue":""},{"word":"past","clue":"the time before now"},{"word":"present","clue":"the time now"},{"word":"ago","clue":"before now (ten years ago = ten years before today)"},{"word":"modern","clue":"new and using the latest ideas"},{"word":"old-fashioned","clue":"not modern; from the past"},{"word":"village","clue":"a very small town in the countryside"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["My Aunt is lebanese.","my aunt is Lebanese","My aunt is Lebanese.","My aunt is lebanese."],"answer":"My aunt is Lebanese.","explanation":"Nationalities start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الجنسيات بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Spot the word that must start with a capital.","options":["city","arabic","language","country"],"answer":"arabic","explanation":"Languages start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"اللغات بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["ziyad speaks English very well.","Ziyad Speaks english very well.","Ziyad speaks English very well.","Ziyad speaks english very well."],"answer":"Ziyad speaks English very well.","explanation":"Languages start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"اللغات بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["the Nile is in Egypt.","The Nile is in egypt.","The nile is in Egypt.","The Nile is in Egypt."],"answer":"The Nile is in Egypt.","explanation":"Cities and countries start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"المدن والدول بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["Bahrain is an island country.","Bahrain is an island Country.","bahrain is an island country.","Bahrain is an Island country."],"answer":"Bahrain is an island country.","explanation":"city, country, language are common nouns – small letters.","explanation_ar":"الكلمات العامة بحرف صغير."},{"q":"How many capital letters are missing? \"my friend is egyptian and speaks arabic.\"","options":["4","2","3","1"],"answer":"3","explanation":"Nationalities start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الجنسيات بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["Hamad is Emirati. He lives in dubai.","Hamad is emirati. He lives in dubai.","Hamad is emirati. He lives in Dubai.","Hamad is Emirati. He lives in Dubai."],"answer":"Hamad is Emirati. He lives in Dubai.","explanation":"Nationalities start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الجنسيات بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Find the word that is NOT a proper noun.","options":["nationality","Urdu","Oman","Saudi"],"answer":"nationality","explanation":"city, country, language are common nouns – small letters.","explanation_ar":"الكلمات العامة بحرف صغير."},{"q":"","options":["We have arabic and Science today.","We have Arabic and science today.","We have Arabic and Science Today.","We have arabic and science today."],"answer":"We have Arabic and science today.","explanation":"Languages start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"اللغات بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["Many Malaysian students study in madinah.","Many Malaysian students study in Madinah.","Many malaysian students study in madinah.","Many malaysian students study in Madinah."],"answer":"Many Malaysian students study in Madinah.","explanation":"Nationalities start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الجنسيات بحرف كبير."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Then and Now” that shows capital letters for cities, countries, nationalities and languages in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Then and Now” that shows capital letters for cities, countries, nationalities and languages in action"},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Builder”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Builder"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Saudi, Egyptian, Arabic: Capitalizing Proper Nouns”. Let’s learn capital letters for cities, countries, nationalities and languages together. In English, nationalities and languages always start with a capital letter: Saudi, Egyptian, Jordanian, Malaysian; Arabic, English, French. This is different from Arabic. In English, nationalities and languages always start with a capital letter: Saudi, Egyptian, Jordanian, Malaysian; Arabic, English, French. This is different from Arabic. Cities and countries also start with a capital letter: Madinah, Saudi Arabia, Egypt, Malaysia. Here are some examples. Yusuf is Egyptian. He was born in Cairo. Lina speaks Arabic and English. Adam is from Kuala Lumpur in Malaysia. Be careful! Some learners say: “My friend is egyptian.” That’s not right. We say: “My friend is Egyptian.” Nationalities need a capital letter. Quick check: Does \"english\" need a capital letter? … Think! … Yes – *English*. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"Saudi\", \"Egyptian\" and \"English\" with capital letters.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS5","title":"My Town Then and Now: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to interview an older person about the past.","Students will be able to write a \"Then and Now\" report about their town.","I can interview someone about the past.","I can write about my town then and now."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من إجراء مقابلة مع شخص كبير في السن عن الماضي.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة تقرير «الماضي والحاضر» عن مدينتهم.","أستطيع أن أجري مقابلة مع شخص عن الماضي.","أستطيع أن أكتب عن مدينتي في الماضي والحاضر."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"past","pos":"noun","ipa":"/pæst/","definition":"the time before now","arabic":"الماضي","example":"In the past, people traveled by camel.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"present","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈprɛzənt/","definition":"the time now","arabic":"الحاضر","example":"In the present, we travel by car and plane.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"ago","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/əˈɡoʊ/","definition":"before now (ten years ago = ten years before today)","arabic":"منذ / قبل","example":"My family moved here five years ago.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"modern","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈmɑdɚn/","definition":"new and using the latest ideas","arabic":"حديث / عصري","example":"Riyadh has many modern towers.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"old-fashioned","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/oʊldˈfæʃənd/","definition":"not modern; from the past","arabic":"قديم الطراز","example":"My grandma has an old-fashioned radio.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"village","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈvɪlədʒ/","definition":"a very small town in the countryside","arabic":"قرية","example":"My grandfather grew up in a mountain village.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"building","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbɪldɪŋ/","definition":"a structure with walls and a roof, like a house or a school","arabic":"مبنى","example":"The new hospital is a tall building.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"stone","pos":"noun","ipa":"/stoʊn/","definition":"a hard material from rocks","arabic":"حجر","example":"The old fort is made of stone.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"mud","pos":"noun","ipa":"/mʌd/","definition":"wet, soft earth","arabic":"طين","example":"Some old houses in Najd were made of mud.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"dusty","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈdʌsti/","definition":"covered with dust; dry and dirty","arabic":"مُغبَرّ","example":"The roads were dusty after the wind.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"narrow","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈnɛroʊ/","definition":"not wide; small from side to side","arabic":"ضيق","example":"The old market has narrow lanes.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"wide","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/waɪd/","definition":"big from side to side","arabic":"واسع / عريض","example":"King Fahd Road is very wide.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"memory","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmɛmɚi/","definition":"something you remember from the past","arabic":"ذكرى","example":"Eid at Grandma's house is my best memory.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 1: was/were, there was/were, questions about the past, then-and-now words and capital letters for places, nationalities and languages.\nA \"Then and Now\" report compares the past with the present. Use In those days…, Long ago…, Nowadays…, Today….\n✔ was/were for the past; is/are for now\n✔ there was / there were for things that existed\n✔ opposites: narrow/wide, quiet/busy\n✔ capitals for cities, countries, nationalities, languages","examples":["In those days, the city was quiet.","There were many farms around the city.","There wasn't an airport.","Nowadays, there are modern hospitals.","My grandma was a Jordanian teacher.","Was there a cinema? – No, there wasn't.","The shops were tiny and dark.","Today, the roads are wide and busy."],"common_errors":["✗ In 1980 Taif is small. → ✓ In 1980, Taif was small. (Past time → was.)","✗ There was many farms. → ✓ There were many farms. (Plural → there were.)","✗ my grandpa is egyptian. → ✓ My grandpa is Egyptian. (Capitals for the first word and nationalities.)"],"arabic":"نراجع was/were وthere was/were وصفات الماضي والحاضر والحروف الكبيرة.\nتقرير «الماضي والحاضر» يقارن: In those days… ثم Nowadays…\nلا تنسَ: was/were للماضي وis/are للحاضر."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “My Town Then and Now: Language in Use”. Let’s learn was/were, there was/were, then-and-now words and capital letters (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L03-U1-LS5 | My Town Then and Now: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Time-machine interview: one student is a grandparent from 1970, the other is a reporter. The reporter asks \"Where were you born? Was there a school? Were there any cars?\" and takes notes.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 1: was/were, there was/were, questions about the past, then-and-now words and capital letters for places, nationalities and languages. A \"Then and Now\" report compares the past with the present. Use In those days…, Long ago…, Nowadays…, Today….","on_screen":"✔ was/were for the past; is/are for now • ✔ there was / there were for things that existed • ✔ opposites: narrow/wide, quiet/busy","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. In those days, the city was quiet. There were many farms around the city. There wasn't an airport.","on_screen":"In those days, the city was quiet. / There were many farms around the city. / There wasn't an airport.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “In 1980 Taif is small.” That’s not right. We say: “In 1980, Taif was small.” Past time → was.","on_screen":"✗ In 1980 Taif is small.   ✓ In 1980, Taif was small.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “There was many farms.”? … Think! … It should be “There were many farms.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can interview someone about the past.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can interview someone about the past.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: was/were, there was/were, then-and-now words and capital letters (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع was/were وthere was/were وصفات الماضي والحاضر والحروف الكبيرة.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: In 1980 Taif is small. — الصحيح: In 1980, Taif was small.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أجري مقابلة مع شخص عن الماضي."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Taif Then and Now – Yusuf","body":"My grandpa came to Taif from Egypt in 1980. In those days, Taif was a small, quiet city.\nThere was a famous market, and there were many rose farms.\nThe roads weren't wide, and there weren't any big malls.\nNowadays, Taif is busy and modern. There are wide roads, new hospitals, and big shopping centers.\nBut the rose farms are still there, and the air is still cool and fresh.\nGrandpa says Taif is his second home!","word_count":77,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Yusuf's report. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Yusuf's grandpa came to Taif from Egypt.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Taif Then and Now – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"In 1980, Taif was a big, noisy city.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Taif Then and Now – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"There were many rose farms.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Taif Then and Now – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"There were big malls in 1980.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Taif Then and Now – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Nowadays, the roads in Taif are wide.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Taif Then and Now – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The rose farms are not there anymore.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Taif Then and Now – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"In 1980, the roads in Taif ___ wide.","options":["didn't","weren't","wasn't","aren't"],"answer":"weren't","explanation":"Past → was/were; now → is/are.","explanation_ar":"الماضي was/were والحاضر is/are."},{"q":"___ a famous market in the old city.","options":["There was","There were","It were","It was"],"answer":"There was","explanation":"One → there was; many → there were.","explanation_ar":"there was للمفرد وthere were للجمع."},{"q":"Nowadays, Taif is busy and ___.","options":["dusty","narrow","ancient","modern"],"answer":"modern","explanation":"Choose the then-and-now word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة."},{"q":"","options":["Yusuf's grandpa is egyptian.","yusuf's grandpa is Egyptian.","Yusuf's grandpa is Egyptian.","Yusuf's Grandpa is egyptian."],"answer":"Yusuf's grandpa is Egyptian.","explanation":"Cities, countries, nationalities and languages → capital letters.","explanation_ar":"الحروف الكبيرة."},{"q":"___ there any malls in 1980? – No, there weren't.","options":["Are","Were","Did","Was"],"answer":"Were","explanation":"Questions: Was/Were + subject…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ was/were."},{"q":"Long ago, the city ___ quiet.","options":["be","were","is","was"],"answer":"was","explanation":"Past → was/were; now → is/are.","explanation_ar":"الماضي was/were والحاضر is/are."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Time-machine interview. Write the reporter's questions and the answers.","items":[{"q":"Ask where he was born.","options":[],"answer":"Where were you born? – I was born in a village near Abha.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses was/were, there was/were, then-and-now words and capital letters (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask about his school.","options":[],"answer":"Was there a school in your village? – Yes, there was a small one.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses was/were, there was/were, then-and-now words and capital letters (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask about cars.","options":[],"answer":"Were there many cars? – No, there weren't. People rode donkeys.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses was/were, there was/were, then-and-now words and capital letters (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask about his favorite game.","options":[],"answer":"What was your favorite game? – It was a stone game with my friends.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses was/were, there was/were, then-and-now words and capital letters (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask if life was difficult.","options":[],"answer":"Was life difficult? – Sometimes, but we were happy.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses was/were, there was/were, then-and-now words and capital letters (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write \"My Town Then and Now\".","items":[{"q":"Plan: 3 facts about the past and 3 about now.","options":[],"answer":"past – small town, one market, no hospital; now – big city, many shops, two hospitals","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses was/were, there was/were, then-and-now words and capital letters (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 6–7 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"In the past, my town was small. There was one market. There wasn't a hospital. Nowadays, it is a big city. There are many shops. There are two hospitals. I love my town!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses was/were, there was/were, then-and-now words and capital letters (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: was/were? there was/were? capitals? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"There was many shops\" to \"There were many shops\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses was/were, there was/were, then-and-now words and capital letters (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Quiz Show Challenge","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Teams take turns choosing a category and a cue word.","Grammar: make a sentence with was/were, there was/were, then-and-now words and capital letters (unit review). Words: give the meaning. Spelling: spell it. Write It!: write a sentence with correct punctuation.","Correct answers score 10 points; teams may steal a question another team misses.","The highest score after 8 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"past","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"present","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"ago","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"modern","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"old-fashioned","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"village","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"building","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"stone","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"mud","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"dusty","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"narrow","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"wide","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"memory","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Fifty years ago, the market ___ very small.","options":["was","were","is","are"],"answer":"was","explanation":"Past → was/were; now → is/are.","explanation_ar":"الماضي was/were والحاضر is/are."},{"q":"","options":["There were many sheeps in the village.","There was many sheep in the village.","It were many sheep in the village.","There were many sheep in the village."],"answer":"There were many sheep in the village.","explanation":"One → there was; many → there were.","explanation_ar":"there was للمفرد وthere were للجمع."},{"q":"The opposite of \"busy\" is ___.","options":["wide","dusty","modern","quiet"],"answer":"quiet","explanation":"Choose the then-and-now word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة."},{"q":"","options":["My Grandmother speaks turkish.","my grandmother speaks Turkish.","My grandmother speaks Turkish.","My grandmother speaks turkish."],"answer":"My grandmother speaks Turkish.","explanation":"Cities, countries, nationalities and languages → capital letters.","explanation_ar":"الحروف الكبيرة."},{"q":"","options":["Were your grandparents born in Taif?","Did your grandparents born in Taif?","Your grandparents were born in Taif?","Was your grandparents born in Taif?"],"answer":"Were your grandparents born in Taif?","explanation":"Questions: Was/Were + subject…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ was/were."},{"q":"___, there are wide roads in our city.","options":["Long ago","In those days","Nowadays","In 1960"],"answer":"Nowadays","explanation":"Choose the then-and-now word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة."},{"q":"There ___ a hospital near the village. People went to the city.","options":["didn't","weren't","isn't","wasn't"],"answer":"wasn't","explanation":"One → there was; many → there were.","explanation_ar":"there was للمفرد وthere were للجمع."},{"q":"","options":["In those days, life was simple.","In those days, life were simple.","In those days, life simple was.","In those days, life is simple."],"answer":"In those days, life was simple.","explanation":"Past → was/were; now → is/are.","explanation_ar":"الماضي was/were والحاضر is/are."},{"q":"Where ___ your father born?","options":["did","was","were","is"],"answer":"was","explanation":"Questions: Was/Were + subject…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ was/were."},{"q":"Choose the best sentence for a \"Then and Now\" report:","options":["Long ago, there were a well, but nowadays there is water pipes.","Long ago, there was a well, but nowadays there are water pipes.","Long ago, there was a well, but nowadays there was water pipes.","Long ago, it was a well, but nowadays there are water pipe."],"answer":"Long ago, there was a well, but nowadays there are water pipes.","explanation":"One → there was; many → there were.","explanation_ar":"there was للمفرد وthere were للجمع."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"Yusuf recording an interview with his grandfather on a tablet in a garden, with an old photo album on the table. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Yusuf recording an interview with his grandfather on a tablet in a garden, with an old photo album on the table"},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Then and Now”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Then and Now”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L03-U1-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Quiz Show Challenge”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Quiz Show Challenge"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS5-T1","script":"My grandpa came to Taif from Egypt in 1980. In those days, Taif was a small, quiet city. There was a famous market, and there were many rose farms. The roads weren't wide, and there weren't any big malls. Nowadays, Taif is busy and modern. There are wide roads, new hospitals, and big shopping centers. But the rose farms are still there, and the air is still cool and fresh. Grandpa says Taif is his second home!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U1-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “My Town Then and Now: Language in Use”. Let’s learn was/were, there was/were, then-and-now words and capital letters (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Time-machine interview: one student is a grandparent from 1970, the other is a reporter. The reporter asks \"Where were you born? Was there a school? Were there any cars?\" and takes notes. Today you use all of Unit 1: was/were, there was/were, questions about the past, then-and-now words and capital letters for places, nationalities and languages. A \"Then and Now\" report compares the past with the present. Use In those days…, Long ago…, Nowadays…, Today…. Here are some examples. In those days, the city was quiet. There were many farms around the city. There wasn't an airport. Be careful! Some learners say: “In 1980 Taif is small.” That’s not right. We say: “In 1980, Taif was small.” Past time → was. Quick check: what is wrong with “There was many farms.”? … Think! … It should be “There were many farms.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can interview someone about the past.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"My great-grandfather ___ a pearl diver.","options":["was","is","were","be"],"answer":"was","explanation":"I / he / she / it / one thing → was.","explanation_ar":"was مع المفرد."},{"q":"The lanes in the old souq ___ narrow.","options":["be","is","was","were"],"answer":"were","explanation":"you / we / they / plural → were.","explanation_ar":"were مع الجمع وyou."},{"q":"Two days ago, it ___ very hot.","options":["be","was","is","were"],"answer":"was","explanation":"Past time words (yesterday, last…, ago) → was/were.","explanation_ar":"كلمات الماضي ← was/were."},{"q":"","options":["We not were at home last night.","We weren't not at home last night.","We weren't at home last night.","We wasn't at home last night."],"answer":"We weren't at home last night.","explanation":"Negative: wasn't / weren't.","explanation_ar":"النفي: wasn't وweren't."},{"q":"The bakery ___ open yesterday. It was a holiday.","options":["not","isn't","weren't","wasn't"],"answer":"wasn't","explanation":"Negative: wasn't / weren't.","explanation_ar":"النفي: wasn't وweren't."},{"q":"___ a big fountain in the old square.","options":["Was there","There were","It was","There was"],"answer":"There was","explanation":"One thing → there was.","explanation_ar":"للمفرد: there was."},{"q":"___ many palm trees around the village.","options":["It were","There was","There were","Were there"],"answer":"There were","explanation":"Many things → there were.","explanation_ar":"للجمع: there were."},{"q":"___ the old fort big? – Yes, it was.","options":["Were","Did","Is","Was"],"answer":"Was","explanation":"Questions: Was/Were + subject…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال يبدأ بـ was أو were."},{"q":"","options":["Where was you on Friday?","Where were you on Friday?","Where were you on Friday was?","Where you were on Friday?"],"answer":"Where were you on Friday?","explanation":"Where/Why/When + was/were + subject?","explanation_ar":"أداة الاستفهام ثم was/were ثم الفاعل."},{"q":"Were there any shops in the village? – No, there ___.","options":["wasn't","weren't","aren't","didn't"],"answer":"weren't","explanation":"Short answers: Yes, it was. / No, they weren't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة."},{"q":"wide ↔ ___","options":["narrow","modern","ancient","quiet"],"answer":"narrow","explanation":"Choose the opposite word.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المضادة."},{"q":"The temples in Egypt are 4,000 years old. They are ___.","options":["ancient","old-fashioned","new","modern"],"answer":"ancient","explanation":"old (not new) • old-fashioned (not modern) • ancient (very, very old).","explanation_ar":"درجات المعنى للقِدم."},{"q":"We moved to Jeddah five years ___.","options":["past","ago","since","before"],"answer":"ago","explanation":"number + time + ago.","explanation_ar":"العدد ثم الوقت ثم ago."},{"q":"Grandma's old-fashioned radio is from the ___.","options":["memory","present","past","future"],"answer":"past","explanation":"Choose the word that fits the meaning.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة للمعنى."},{"q":"The roads were ___ after the sandstorm.","options":["wide","dusty","ancient","modern"],"answer":"dusty","explanation":"Choose the word that fits the meaning.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة للمعنى."},{"q":"Something you remember is a ___.","options":["memory","building","stone","village"],"answer":"memory","explanation":"Choose the word that fits the meaning.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة للمعنى."},{"q":"","options":["My best friend is Sudanese.","My Best friend is sudanese.","My best friend is sudanese.","my best friend is Sudanese"],"answer":"My best friend is Sudanese.","explanation":"Nationalities start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الجنسيات بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["Do you Speak urdu?","Do you speak urdu?","Do you speak Urdu?","do you speak Urdu?"],"answer":"Do you speak Urdu?","explanation":"Languages start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"اللغات بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["Amman Is in jordan.","Amman is in Jordan.","amman is in Jordan.","Amman is in jordan."],"answer":"Amman is in Jordan.","explanation":"Cities and countries start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"المدن والدول بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["Oman is a beautiful Country.","oman is a beautiful country.","Oman is a Beautiful country.","Oman is a beautiful country."],"answer":"Oman is a beautiful country.","explanation":"city, country, language are common nouns – small letters.","explanation_ar":"الكلمات العامة بحرف صغير."},{"q":"How many capital letters are missing? \"ali is iraqi and speaks english.\"","options":["2","4","3","1"],"answer":"3","explanation":"Nationalities start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الجنسيات بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for a history report:","options":["In 1950, there are no paved roads in the village.","In 1950 there were no paved road in the village.","In 1950, there was no paved roads in the village.","In 1950, there were no paved roads in the village."],"answer":"In 1950, there were no paved roads in the village.","explanation":"Many things → there were.","explanation_ar":"للجمع: there were."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"in the past my town is quiet.\"","options":["In the past, my town was quiet.","in the past, my town was quiet.","In the past my town were quiet.","In the past, my town is quiet."],"answer":"In the past, my town was quiet.","explanation":"Past time words (yesterday, last…, ago) → was/were.","explanation_ar":"كلمات الماضي ← was/were."},{"q":"Was the trip to Al-Ula fun? – ___","options":["Yes, was it amazing!","Yes, it were amazing!","Yes, it was amazing!","Yes, it is amazing yesterday!"],"answer":"Yes, it was amazing!","explanation":"Short answers: Yes, it was. / No, they weren't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة."}],"theme_ar":"الماضي والحاضر","essential_question_ar":"كيف تغيّرت الحياة في بلدنا عبر الزمن؟","can_do":"I can describe people, places and things in the past with was, were, there was and there were.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أصف الناس والأماكن والأشياء في الماضي باستخدام was وwere وthere was وthere were."});
